Restores drop-on-empty-strip-space appending, lost when e90850e moved tabs to
dnd-kit. User flagged it: a pane created by 'Split active tab right' holds one
tab and a wide empty strip, so losing that target makes split panes awkward.

How: each strip is a createDroppable with type 'workspace-tab-strip' carrying
its paneId in data. handleTabDragOver checks for it before falling through to
move(), because move() only understands sortable-to-sortable and cannot express
'append past the end'.

Two settings matter and are easy to get wrong:
- collisionPriority: CollisionPriority.Lowest. The strip contains the tabs, so
  without this it can win collisions against the tab under the pointer and every
  hover would read as an append.
- collisionDetector: pointerIntersection. Shape-based detection on a full-width
  strip overlaps everything.

Compact strip: its drop zone targets panes[panes.length-1] because that strip
flattens every pane's tabs, so trailing space can only sensibly mean the last
pane. This matches the old compactStripDragOver. The consequence is that
appending to the END of a non-last pane from the compact strip is no longer
expressible - there is no empty space between one pane's tabs and the next
pane's in a flattened strip. The old code resolved that with a 'right half of
the last tab' heuristic that sortable semantics have no equivalent for. I
retargeted that test rather than fake the behaviour; pane strips (the case the
user cared about) fully support trailing append.

Trap that cost time and will again: splitPane CLONES the active tab with a
fresh workspaceId('tab') into the new pane - see splitPane, not
moveTabToNewSplit. So after a split the same TITLE legitimately appears in two
panes with different ids. I read that as a duplication bug and nearly 'fixed'
intended split-view semantics. Assert on ids, or expect the repeated title.

Still NOT VERIFIED on WebKit - same limitation as e90850e. 164 e2e tests pass
in Chromium on Linux, including a split-then-drop-into-empty-strip regression
test, but the macOS behaviour this whole line of work targets is unconfirmed.
